<title>UK: Black Sea Novorossiisk oil port shut.</title>
<headline>Black Sea Novorossiisk oil port shut.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Black Sea port of Novorossiisk, Russia's main crude export outlet, is shut to tanker loading because of high swell, a shipping source said on Friday.</p>
<p>The port has been shut since 2110 hours local time on Thursday as swells averaged between 1.3 and two metres, the source said.</p>
<p>On Friday morning, there was one crude tanker at the berth and one at anchor.</p>
<p>All other Black Sea and Baltic ports exporting Russian oil were operating normally on Friday, the source said.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 6280</p>
</text>
